# b5-refactor-r2: comment.go:149 link+tabs compute urlOf(r) twice for every realm bullet.
#
# Each bullet is built as `link(urlOf(r), r) + tabs(base, r)`, and tabs calls urlOf(pkgPath)
# again on the same argument; the three bullet sites (44, 63, 80) spell the concatenation
# out by hand, and the one at 44 silently omits tabs. One realmItem(base, pkgPath) computes
# urlOf once and carries all three: the link closure (6 lines) and tabs (8) become one
# 8-line function, 196 -> 191 lines. The gnoweb branch gains the source/help shortcuts the
# other two branches already have, which is the only output change.
#
# Repro from a plain clone:
#   git clone https://github.com/gnolang/gno && cd gno
#   git checkout ecf7af0f29abe4737a52803d672bc5a33c17cc60
#   git apply <path to this file>
#   cd misc/gnopreview && gofmt -l . && go vet ./... && go test ./...
# Measured at ecf7af0f2 with go1.25.9: gofmt silent, vet silent,
#   "ok  github.com/gnolang/gno/misc/gnopreview  0.004s"
